  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read in JBIG2Bitmap::combine()\n     (JBIG2Stream.cc) via a crafted JBIG2 stream, from a misplaced isOk check\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-32365.patch: add the isOk() guard at the top of\n       JBIG2Bitmap::combine() so every caller is protected against\n       out-of-bounds reads on a not-OK bitmap (upstream commit 1f151565,\n       adapted to poppler 0.62 GBool/Guint)\n     - CVE-2025-32365\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: uncontrolled recursion / stack overflow in the XRefStm\n     chain parser (XRef.cc) via a crafted PDF, causing denial of service\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2020-23804.patch: cap the XRefStm chain at 4096\n       entries in XRef::readXRefTable() to stop the readXRef/readXRefTable\n       recursion from exhausting the stack on crafted PDFs (upstream commit\n       ec8a43c8)\n     - CVE-2020-23804",
